  "question": {
    "text": "The half-life of a radioactive nucleus is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math> years. The fraction of the original sample that would decay in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>15</mn></math> years is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "n4GMj",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dD8rU",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "xNeSW",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "tzZzW",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the number of half lives covered by the radioactive material is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>t</mi><msub><mi>T</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msub></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Substitute the values of the known parameters into equation (1) to calculate the number of half lives covered.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>n</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mn>15</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>years</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>years</mi></mrow></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The relation between the amount of radioactive substance after certain time can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Substitute the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;into equation (2) to obtain the fraction of the remaining substance.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mi>N</mi></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8658;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>Hence, the amount of the decayed substance can be written as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p></blockquote>",
